  "rust_authorities": "Rust now owns accepted friendships/blocks, tag schema/CSPRNG allocation/lookup, Unicode16 NFC/full case folding, public roster projections, role/consent gates, quotas/replay and transactional SQL. Actual native account capabilities fence every protected continuation. SQL block epochs include other connections; the bounded native cache publishes after owned commit and bypasses outer transactions. Rust also owns private friend-file payloads/fingerprints/revisions, outbox selection/retry/CAS and opaque commit-bound upload claims. Payload SHA256 is verified before a claim is issued. Selection commits before SDK IO; outer uncommitted snapshots cannot publish; native revision/PUID checks preserve superseded state and cancellation/retry. Worker read-back parsing runs in Rust. The actual cached-block, outer-commit, revoked-provider, cloud transaction, uncommitted publication and corrupt-digest controls are red before the respective fixes and green afterwards. These are modern native service policies, not original Live friend/collation recovery. Trusted canonical/provider identity, Discord voice preferences, Steam upstream policy, generic HTTP/file/process/SDK IO and complete Rust service replacement, cross-store/process recovery and full original/native played/delivered gates remain open.",
  "reproduced_gaps": [
    {
